{{page dlc|r+}}

'''Online''' is an in-development mode exclusive to the Repentance DLC and PC that allows players to play Co-Op with other people on different devices. Players may choose to play with friends on Steam or be randomly matched with other players.

Online mode is currently available with ''[[The Binding of Isaac: Repentance+|Repentance+]]''. The initial plan was to open the beta the first two weeks of every month but Tyrone made the decision on February 2, 2024 to shut down the beta.<ref>https://twitter.com/tyronerodriguez/status/1753273950124343484</ref>

'''WARNING:''' Repentance+ online co-op is still in a beta state. It may be unstable and can sometimes corrupt your save data. Play it at your own risk. You can always turn off Repentance+ content in Steam's DLC manager, and the game keeps a backup of your pre-Repentance+ save files.

== Changes ==
Online mode uses most of the same game rules as [[Repentance Co-Op]] but with the following changes:
* Destroying {{r|Boss Room}} items through {{i|Abyss}}, {{i|Eternal D6}}, {{c|Tainted Cain}}, {{i|Void}} etc., will no longer prevent further items from spawning.
** Silver Treasure Room items in [[Greed Mode|Greed]]/Greedier mode behave the same as Boss Room items.
* Co-Op Ghosts can fly over pits and obstacles, open {{e|Chest}}s and {{e|Grab Bag}}s, and pick up {{e|Penny|text=Pennies}}, {{e|Bomb}}s, and {{e|Key}}s.
** Co-Op Ghosts have their damage reduced to 20% and their other stats are reverted to base.
** Co-Op Ghosts can revive themselves by picking up an {{e|Eternal Heart}}.
* Giving coins to {{m|Revive Machine}}s will revive dead players without needing to beat a boss, requiring 10 coins for the first revival.
* When moving to another room, the door entered is closed for one second.
* Enemies and bosses, such as {{e|Eye}}, {{e|The Bloat}}, or {{e|Gabriel}}, now have an indicator on where they will fire their laser beam in rooms larger than a regular 1x1 room.
* Players can communicate through a chat-box or through the [[Emote Wheel]].
* Players can restart a run if all players hold down the R button.
* Upon successfully completing a run, all players will be sent to a [[Deathmatch]] mini-game.
* Following a run's end, each player is given a select list of "Sins" which are titles that are given depending on the player's actions that run. The amount of times a player has earned a Sin can be checked in the Stats page.
* Full list of Sins: {{column list | width = 30em | content =
